minios-gui (1.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Exclude remaining Debian build and test artifacts
  * Add xauth for the Xvfb-based build test suite
  * Add the GdkPixbuf SVG loader required by document rendering tests
  * Make Mermaid document rendering deterministic

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 19:45:00 +0300

minios-gui (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add DocumentTextView for native GTK rendering of precompiled MiniOS markup
    documents without a Markdown, HTML or JavaScript engine at runtime.
  * Render compiled headings, lists, code, links and anchors through TextBuffer,
    and embed responsive native tables plus SVG/image assets through GTK child
    widgets.
  * Let HelpPopoverButton display compiled documents through document= while
    keeping its existing plain-text and Pango-markup help modes.
  * Remove the unpublished runtime Markdown/Mistune and native Mermaid-subset
    APIs; Markdown and Mermaid are build-time source formats for applications.
  * Keep the compiled document renderer compatible with Python 3.6 and GTK 3.22.
  * Add tests for document schema validation, links, responsive native tables,
    SVG assets and compiled-document help popovers.
  * Provide one shared Node.js Markdown/Mermaid compiler with a pinned npm
    lockfile for applications that prepare compiled help bundles before release.
  * Highlight fenced code at build time with the same Shiki 2.5.0
    github-light/github-dark themes used by the current VitePress documentation.
  * Render code blocks as responsive, selectable content-column widgets and
    scale compiled Mermaid SVG diagrams to the available document width.
  * Run the complete GTK and CSS test suite under Xvfb during package builds.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:20:00 +0300

minios-gui (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Honor cancellation requested before CommandRunner finishes spawning the
    child process instead of letting the newly started command continue.
  * Add shared manager-state row sizing and active/running/available edge
    semantics for consistent manager lists.
  * Use a brighter green active/current row accent without changing success
    banners and badges.
  * Add reusable canonical HeaderBar and semantic StatusBanner helpers for
    MiniOS GTK applications.
  * Add shared compact module presentation metadata and byte formatting used by
    Installer, Module Manager, and Image Builder UI.
  * Standardize horizontal padding for text and icon+text buttons while keeping
    icon-only HeaderBar and embedded ComboBox/SpinButton controls compact.
  * Add TokenCompletionPopover for token-aware static or asynchronous completion
    with an arrow anchored to the current entry token; Up/Down choose a result,
    Tab or Enter accepts it, Escape closes the list, and Shift+Tab keeps normal
    backward focus navigation.
  * Add HelpPopoverButton for keyboard-accessible contextual help, supporting
    compact field explanations and wider structured page-level guidance with
    formatted Pango markup.
  * Rely on gir1.2-gtk-3.0 for both Gtk and Gdk introspection data instead of
    the nonexistent gir1.2-gdk-3.0 package.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:25:00 +0300

minios-gui (1.0.0) bionic; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: canonical MiniOS GUI stylesheet shared by all minios-*
    GTK applications and driveutility.
  * Build python3-minios-gui from the same source repository, providing
    Python 3.6-compatible styling, icon, dialog and command helpers.

